Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["DR2MS", "ObjectName",
 CellID->620540953,ExpressionUUID->"92304d3e-b91c-4a6e-84f3-2f6d39741fd2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"a48daaa3-759d-4641-8cd6-2257408b588f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["DR2MS",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DR2MS"], "[", 
   StyleBox["lag", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ca4b3ebe-0c6d-4cf8-b65a-c20d1ef622a8"],
 " takes the renormalizable Lagrangian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["lag", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e699499-da9c-4c2c-8553-1431ee55d615"],
 " that is renormalized in dimensional reduction using the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["DR", "_"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "09b5e55f-80de-4e83-a419-92ca175e77a1"],
 "  scheme as input and returns the version of that Lagrangian renormalized \
using dimensional regularization in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["MS", "_"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c45c22c-1536-4ff1-a07a-9b0931b98b83"],
 " scheme by incorporating the appropriate finite counterterms required for \
the scheme change. "
}], "Usage",
 CellID->1251207239,ExpressionUUID->"43c1ffe0-c549-40ed-aa8d-3663cbd8ebfa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The argument ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["lag", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "60f7a0ba-4c7f-4c3b-9e5d-8f402648cecb"],
 " must be a valid Lagrangian containing only renormalizable interactions. \
Non-renormalizable interactions are currently not supported. In addition, the \
shift is only performed for Lagrangian terms that can contribute to the \
tree-level matching of the theory. Finite counterterms for interactions that \
only contribute at the loop level are not included as these appear only as a \
two-loop effect in the corresponding EFT."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->1869578717,ExpressionUUID->"1c9e66db-b210-4230-b5b4-668458ec43d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This function then loops over all relevant Lagrangian terms and includes \
the finite scheme change counterterms following ",
 ButtonBox["Martin and Vaughn (1993) [hep-ph/9308222]",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9308222"], None}],
 "."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->866870056,ExpressionUUID->"8a2df598-2c53-491c-83f3-a8a446d53d7e"],

Cell["\<\
The finite counterterms for the gauge couplings are immediately absorbed into \
a redefinition of these gauge couplings to achieve a canonical normalization \
of the kinetic terms of the gauge fields.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->198320321,ExpressionUUID->"60c57069-b879-447c-a9f2-33879d37e3e8"]
}, Open  ]],

